From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiaoge-tou <85100527+Tiaoge-tou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:53:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Both games decode BC on the CPU: tex_bc_cpu on in their
 profiles

Silksong and Hades II opt into patch 0008's CPU BC decode (patch port 0086, closing the port queue), so a GPU without BC texture support (an iPhone 13 Pro's A15, any A15/A16 device) runs them: the device check in main.m refuses only a game whose profile does not decode on the CPU. Without the row both games would be turned away at start on exactly the device class PROJECT.md's Phase 4 verifies on. The row is this tree's own key (game.py), not one of the ported ones; nothing else changes.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Silksong and Hades II run on GPUs without BC support, through patch 0008's CPU decode (PROJECT.md Phase 4)
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 2

---
 dm/games/010013C00E930000/game.tsv | 2 ++
 dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/games/010013C00E930000/game.tsv b/dm/games/010013C00E930000/game.tsv
index 3c4a829..fd22f3c 100644
--- a/dm/games/010013C00E930000/game.tsv
+++ b/dm/games/010013C00E930000/game.tsv
@@ -66,3 +66,5 @@ serve_patch	n:menu_title.bundle@6E3E5C:41030A3D>4129C10A@6EAA5C:00000000>401ADB3
 display_hz	120
 # The launcher's button-skin toggle for this game (settings.tsv DM_SILK_SKIN): the pad's image skin, or its glass controls
 pad_skin_toggle	on
+# BC textures are decoded on the CPU (patch 0008's route), so a GPU without BC support (an A15 or A16 iPhone, an older iPad) runs this game: the device check in main.m lets a tex_bc_cpu game through
+tex_bc_cpu	on
diff --git a/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv b/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv
index de78df6..2240f7a 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv
+++ b/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv
@@ -49,6 +49,9 @@ display_wide	on
 # Whether this engine follows past 60 is unmeasured (it has no hle_fpslock row for its build yet): an experiment, 2026-10-27.
 display_hz	120
 
+# BC textures are decoded on the CPU (patch 0008's route), so a GPU without BC support (an A15 or A16 iPhone, an older iPad) runs this game: the device check in main.m lets a tex_bc_cpu game through
+tex_bc_cpu	on
+
 # ---- Memory ----
 # The NPDM declares no system resource (META +0x14 = 0): the game uses SetHeapSize. It asks for 3.10 GB (pool − used memory), which the 3.25 GB heap region of
 # the 4 GB layout holds. main carries an 82 MB bss: the rewritten modules take more than the default 64 MB of used memory, so SetHeapSize(pool − 64 MB) would not fit
